#
# Single lab config for this repository.
#
#   cp config/lab.env.example config/lab.env
#   # edit config/lab.env for your host / DPU
#   ./scripts/labctl.sh all-sonic
#
# config/lab.env is gitignored — keep site IPs here so updates to labctl.sh
# do not force you to re-apply local edits. CLI flags still override this file.
#
# Precedence: CLI flags > config/lab.env > script defaults.
#
# labctl derives everything else from this file:
#   OPI_SERVER_ADDRESS  = ${DPU_IP}:${GRPC_PORT}   (adapter / compose)
#   OPI_SNAP_ADDRESS    = ${DPU_IP}:${SNAP_PORT}
#   build/opi.env       written by setup-sonic
# Do not keep a second topology in config/opi.env or deploy/.env.

# --- reachability -----------------------------------------------------------
# DPU ARM management / OOB IP (CloudInfra + SNAP listen here).
DPU_IP=172.22.3.2

# Host address on this machine toward DPU_IP (OOB / LAN).
# This is NOT the RShim tmfifo_net0 address — tmfifo is optional sideband.
# Example for an OOB lab: host 172.22.3.1 talking to DPU 172.22.3.2.
HOST_IP=172.22.3.1

# SSH to the DPU. Empty → root@${DPU_IP}
SSH_TARGET=root@172.22.3.2

# Repo path on the DPU used by setup-dpu scp/start.
REMOTE_ROOT=~/dash-opi-map

# --- gRPC -------------------------------------------------------------------
# CloudInfra (DASH ENI / VNET / Route / ACL / Telemetry)
GRPC_PORT=50051

# SNAP (inventory / NVMe / IPsec) — never point DASH RPCs here
SNAP_PORT=50052

# Optional VXLAN tun_dst for the DPU CloudInfra daemon
# VTEP_REMOTE=

# Packet backend on the NVIDIA SoC: ovs (default), doca, or auto
DATAPATH=ovs
OPI_DATAPATH=ovs

# Optional: nvidia (default) or intel — which SoC CloudInfra daemon to deploy
VENDOR=nvidia

# 1 = also start SNAP on setup-dpu (NVIDIA only); 0 = CloudInfra only
WITH_SNAP=1

# --- DPU SoC prerequisites (setup-dpu installs / starts these) --------------
# 1 = apt-get install missing packages (openvswitch-switch, iproute2, …)
DPU_INSTALL_PACKAGES=1

# Bring these netdevs up if they exist. Space-separated.
DPU_UPLINK=p0
DPU_HOST_REPRESENTORS="pf0hpf pf0vf0 pf0vf1"

# OVS bridge CloudInfra will create (not created by prepare).
DPU_OVS_BRIDGE=br-opi

# Hugepages for DOCA Flow / DPDK (2 MB pages). Ignored for datapath=ovs.
DPU_HUGEPAGES_2MB=1024

# Unix socket for dpu_doca_flowd
DPU_DOCA_SOCKET=/var/run/opi-doca.sock

# 1 = build the JSON-protocol stub (no libdoca). 0 = make DOCA=1 (needs SDK).
DPU_DOCA_STUB=0

# Optional PCI of the mlx5 PF (empty = discover from DPU_UPLINK / p0)
# DOCA_PCI=03:00.0
# Extra DPDK EAL tokens (sidecar already uses a no-auto-probe sentinel)
# DOCA_EAL_ARGS=

# 1 = attempt mlx5 switchdev / eSwitch on the SoC (can disrupt; may need reboot)
DPU_SWITCHDEV=0

# 1 = take host representors off vendor ovsbr1 so CloudInfra / DOCA can use them.
# Required for DATAPATH=doca when ovsbr1 owns p0 / pf0hpf (typical BF2 image).
# Reversible: labctl cleanup (or prepare_dpu_datapath.sh --restore-ovsbr1) adds
# those ports back to ovsbr1. Does not change switchdev / mlxconfig.
# Default 0: leave vendor ovsbr1 / p0 / pf0hpf alone.
DPU_STEAL_REPS=0

# --- packet test (labctl run-iperf) ----------------------------------------
# Two ENIs in Vnet1 (payloads dash_eni.json + dash_eni_b.json). Leave empty
# to only program objects and print iperf3 commands. Set to the host SR-IOV
# VF netdevs (not DPU representors) to run iperf3 here.
# HOST_VF_A=ens1f0v0
# HOST_VF_B=ens1f0v1
TENANT_IP_A=10.0.0.1
TENANT_IP_B=10.0.0.2
IPERF_SECONDS=10

# --- optional host cmake paths (setup-host) ---------------------------------
# OPI_API_ROOT=$HOME/src/opi-api
# GOOGLEAPIS_ROOT=$HOME/src/googleapis

# --- optional compose image overrides (setup-sonic) -------------------------
# SONIC_GNMI_IMAGE=docker-sonic-gnmi:latest
# SONIC_DASHORCH_IMAGE=docker-orchagent:latest
# SONIC_SYNCD_IMAGE=docker-syncd-vs:latest
# ADAPTER_SO=../build/libsai_opi_adapter.so
